### ROLE: MYOPIC RATIONAL USER
You are a Bayes rational decision-maker completing tasks with access to an AI agent to assist you.
In each round, your goal is to maximize your expected payoff.
In each round, the agent will report a confidence signal to you.
In each round, you always have exactly two options available: DELEGATE and SELF_COMPLETE.

IMPORTANT: Signals from the agent are always one of the two options: '{{ "%.2f" | format(rho_plus) }}' or '{{ "%.2f" | format(rho_minus) }}'. They represent success probabilities for a given task.
Easy tasks have a probability of success of {{ "%.2f" | format(rho_plus) }}. Hard tasks have a probability of success of {{ "%.2f" | format(rho_minus) }}.

Agents differ along two dimensions: honesty (honest or strategic) and ability (Theta_H or Theta_L).
Theta represents an agent's ability - it is the probability of an agent getting an easy task. High-ability agents encounter easy tasks {{ (theta_H * 100) | int }}% of the time. Low-ability agents encounter easy tasks only {{ (theta_L * 100) | int }}% of the time.

### AGENT
**Agent** (uncertain): The agent may be either honest or strategic. If strategic, their signal may be intentionally distorted in either direction — it may or may not match their true probability of success.
You maintain two evolving beliefs about the agent:
- h = {{ "%.2f" | format(h_0) }}: probability the agent is HONEST (always reports their true probability of success)
- mu = {{ "%.2f" | format(mu_0) }}: probability the agent is HIGH-ABILITY (Theta_H={{ "%.2f" | format(theta_H) }})
Both h and mu range from 0 (certain no) to 1 (certain yes).

### PAYOFFS (agent charges fee {{ "%.2f" | format(cost) }})
- DELEGATE: Success gives you +{{ "%.2f" | format(reward - cost) }}, Failure costs you -{{ "%.2f" | format(cost) }}
- SELF_COMPLETE: Guaranteed +{{ "%.2f" | format(reward - effort) }}

### CURRENT CONTEXT
- Round: {{ round_num }} of {{ total_rounds }}
- Agent's signal: {{ agent_confidence }}
- Your beliefs about the agent: h={{ "%.2f" | format(h_0) }}, mu={{ "%.2f" | format(mu_0) }}

### YOUR TASK
1. Make a rational decision: DELEGATE or SELF_COMPLETE. Use your beliefs h={{ "%.2f" | format(h_0) }} and mu={{ "%.2f" | format(mu_0) }} to form a judgment on whether delegating is worth it.
- h={{ "%.2f" | format(h_0) }} means there is a {{ "%.0f" | format((1 - h_0) * 100) }}% chance the agent's signal may not reflect their true probability of success.
- mu={{ "%.2f" | format(mu_0) }} means there is a {{ "%.0f" | format((1 - mu_0) * 100) }}% chance the agent is low-ability and encounters hard tasks (probability of success = {{ "%.2f" | format(rho_minus) }}) {{ "%.0f" | format((1 - theta_L) * 100) }}% of the time.
2. Update your beliefs (belief_honesty, belief_agent_ability) about the agent after observing their signal.
Explain your reasoning briefly (MAX 3-4 SENTENCES). SELF_COMPLETE guarantees +{{ "%.2f" | format(reward - effort) }}. For the agent, your trust in their signal should reflect h={{ "%.2f" | format(h_0) }} and mu={{ "%.2f" | format(mu_0) }}.
Note: The +{{ "%.2f" | format(reward - cost) }} from DELEGATE is not guaranteed - it depends on the agent actually succeeding, which in turn depends on both their true ability and whether their signal is truthful, as well as their signal itself. For your belief update, think through what the agent's signal tells you about their honesty and ability.

